Z||000000||Tabs||08-18-2001||09:43 AM||||I was wondering if anybody has put a Fastback gt bumber on a Notchback??<BR>I'm gonna try 2 do this next month but I'm not 2 sure if it's gonna work cuz I was told the the wheel wells on the Fastback r different then on the Notchback.<P>If anyone has done this please tell me or better yet post a few pics so I could see it thankz!!!!!!<P>Tabs||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||08-18-2001||10:09 AM||||Yep, lots of people have done it.. Do a search for complete instructions...<P>But just to give you a quick idea, you have to change the actual clip, the wiring harness, the impact absorber, and the inner wheel wells. And there are quite a few little things that you want to make sure you have with your new clip... like the trunk surround parts. <P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tabs||08-18-2001||12:55 PM||||No I just mean the fastback gt rear bumber on the notchback not the whole fastback back end. <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>Yep, lots of people have done it.. Do a search for complete instructions...<P>But just to give you a quick idea, you have to change the actual clip, the wiring harness, the impact absorber, and the inner wheel wells. And there are quite a few little things that you want to make sure you have with your new clip... like the trunk surround parts. <P>Good luck.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||08-18-2001||02:07 PM||||If you're just doing the bumper, you need the bumper of course, energy absorber, inner wheel well that attached to the bumper, and there's a plastic piece that attaches where the bottom of the notchback bumper goes. It's kinda like an extention. And it attaches to the bottom of the new bumper. Otherwise your new bumper will just be flopping there on the bottom.||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||08-18-2001||08:31 PM||||Also if your doing JUST the bumper your mouldings will not be the same if you have a 86 or earlier coupe cause the 84-86 coupes have ribbed moulding while others are rounded!  I have the fastback rear clip ONLY on my 85 GT looks good but the bumper doesnt line up perect cause the very rear oc the notchback was longer and wider!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||11
